      "mergedPostDetails": "I already tried to address this issue in a bug report I made a while ago, however it seems that it has been overlooked, whether it's because it wasn't important enough, not explained clear enough by me (excuse me for my poor english), it has already been considered and I'm not addressing something new (even though I didn't see anyone talk about it), or for whatever reason, but this is understandable considering the pressure put on the devs and the various issues they're already working on (even though I think is a major/important issue).\n\nI apologize for the long introduction and I'll dive straight into the issue without any further ado.\n\nThe issue is that basically my voice in vrchat is too low, even though the microphone strength is set on 100% and the mic activation threshold is set on 0, my voice barely passes the threshold, I tested many times, when I open my mic and try to say something to my friends, either they don't hear anything, or they hear \"something\" when I raise my voice, but they do not hear me saying \"hello? Can you hear me?\", they don't hear any clear words, they probably hear faint muffled sound, and by \"when I raise my voice\" I meant when I raise my voice till the point that I sound like I'm scolding my little sibling in real life, this is how \"low\" my voice is picked up in vrchat.\n\nI've tried many ways to check if I can fix the issue on my end, tried changing many settings, different mic input types (wireless/bluetooth, wired), I cleared cache, data, reinstalled the app, but nothing was fixed.\n\nMy phone details:\n\n-Device Name: Honor 200\n\n-RAM: 12 GB RAM\n\n-Model: ELI-NX9\n\n-Android Version: 15\n\nI apologize for the wall of text, thought that an in detail explanation was required, If there is anything missing or anything that you want me to add please let me know, and thanks for your continuous hard work.",
